Third-party data sources, APIs and tile providers

The MIT license above covers the source code of this project only. The data
sets, APIs and map tiles listed below are provided by third parties under
their own terms; please consult each provider's license before reuse.

Data sources
- Hansen/UMD/Google/USGS/NASA Global Forest Change (GFC-2024 v1.12, GFC-2023
  v1.11) – tree cover 2000 and annual loss year, 30 m (CC BY 4.0)
  https://glad.earthengine.app/view/global-forest-change
  https://storage.googleapis.com/earthenginepartners-hansen/GFC-2024-v1.12/download.html
- WRI / Global Forest Watch – Forest Carbon Flux model (Harris et al. 2021,
  Gibbs et al. 2025), 30 m gross emissions / removals / net flux (CC BY 4.0)
  https://data.globalforestwatch.org/documents/gfw::forest-greenhouse-gas-net-flux/about
- Statistik Austria – Holzeinschlag (timber harvest) by federal state,
  2001–2024; municipality boundaries (Gemeindegrenzen) and population
  https://www.statistik.at/statistiken/land-und-forstwirtschaft/land-und-forstwirtschaftliche-betriebe/holzeinschlag
  https://www.statistik.at/services/tools/services/regionales/regionale-gliederungen
  https://www.data.gv.at/
- Bundesministerium für Land- und Forstwirtschaft, Klima- und Umweltschutz,
  Regionen und Wasserwirtschaft (BML/BMLUK) – Holzeinschlagsmeldung
  https://www.bmluk.gv.at/
- preise.agrarforschung.at (AgrarMarkt Austria / LK Landwirtschaftskammern /
  Statistik Austria / WIFO, HWWI, CME) – timber, pellet and futures price
  series via https://preise.agrarforschung.at/api/getcontent
  https://preise.agrarforschung.at/
- EU Emissions Trading System (EU ETS) – historical EUA carbon prices used for
  the hypothetical ETS liability
  https://climate.ec.europa.eu/eu-action/eu-emissions-trading-system-eu-ets_en

Map tiles and front-end libraries
- CARTO basemaps (light_all) – https://carto.com/basemaps/
- OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL) – https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
- Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause) – https://leafletjs.com/
- Alpine.js (MIT) – https://alpinejs.dev/

Libraries used in processing
- GDAL/OGR (MIT/X) – https://gdal.org/
- NumPy (BSD-3-Clause) – https://numpy.org/
